3.2.m:
Ever devoted to their own duty and devoted to their own work.
Āṅgirasa, Aṃbarīṣa, and Yauvanāśva next;
And Śāntā here is the goddess, the bestower of peace in pacification rites.
Thus ends the fifty-fifth locality. (55)
Thus to you have been told the gotras, and likewise the localities,
And likewise the pravaras of the brahmins here, O scorcher of foes.
Beyond this, I shall speak of the knowers of the three Vedas, O scorcher of foes.
And their own places have been declared by me in due order.
The first place is Śīlā, and Maṇḍorā is the second;
Evaḍī is the third, and Gundarāṇā the fourth;
Kalyāṇīyā is the fifth, and likewise Degāmā the sixth;
Nāyakapurā the seventh, and likewise Ḍalīā the eighth;
Kaḍovyā the ninth, and likewise Kohāṭoyā the tenth;
Haraḍīyā the eleventh, and likewise Bhadukīyā the twelfth;
And here Samprāṇāvā and Kandarāvā are proclaimed;
Vāsarovā is the thirteenth, and Śaraṇḍāvā the fourteenth;
